{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:ClimaxVolumeMass.SkeinCrossingAsymmetryProp","@type":"LeanModule","name":"ClimaxVolumeMass.SkeinCrossingAsymmetryProp","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.skein_crossing_asymmetry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.skein_crossing_asymmetry","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/skein-crossing-asymmetry-prop.lean#L64-L81","doc":"**Skein crossing asymmetry ⇒ Coulomb repulsion.**\n\nIn the substrate regime `q > 1` the `R`-matrix weights the positive\ncrossing (`q`) strictly more than the negative crossing (`q⁻¹`):\n`q⁻¹ < q`.  This crossing-weight asymmetry is exactly the per-crossing\nCoulomb correction `δ = ½(q − q⁻¹) > 0` (relative to the mixed-charge\nbaseline `½(q + q⁻¹)`).  All three conjuncts are *derived* from `q > 1`\n(no unused hypothesis: the weight asymmetry, the correction identity,\nand the positivity each follow from the single premise). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:skein-crossing-asymmetry","label":"prop:skein-crossing-asymmetry","md":"quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/skein-crossing-asymmetry-prop.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.coulombCorrection_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.coulombCorrection_pos","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/skein-crossing-asymmetry-prop.lean#L52-L62","doc":"**Coulomb repulsion at `q > 1`.**\n\nFor the substrate regime `q > 1` the per-crossing correction is\nstrictly positive — the emergent Coulomb repulsion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.coulombCorrection_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.coulombCorrection_eq","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/skein-crossing-asymmetry-prop.lean#L43-L50","doc":"**Coulomb-correction identity.**\n\nThe repulsive correction `q − ½(q + q⁻¹)` relative to the mixed-charge\nbaseline `½(q + q⁻¹)` equals the antisymmetric Skein weight\n`½(q − q⁻¹)`.  Pure `ring` rearrangement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.coulombCorrection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.coulombCorrection","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/climax-volume-mass/skein-crossing-asymmetry-prop.lean#L40-L41","doc":"The per-crossing Coulomb correction `δ = ½(q − q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}